    <bpmn:process id="W_W4681" name="W4681. Executive Protection Program Design &amp; Close-Protection Operations" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Principal daily operations; threat-level change; event
Frequency: Continuous (daily EP detail)
Volume: ~3–6 principals under routine EP (C-suite + family); details per principal
Owner: EP Lead / CSO
Participants: EP agents, principals&#x27; offices, drivers (W4683), GSOC (W4676)
Source: workflow W4681 — Executive Protection Program Design &amp; Close-Protection Operations</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4681_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4681_Lane1" name="EP Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4681_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4681_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4681_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4681_Lane2" name="EP Agents">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4681_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4681_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4681_Start4" name="Principal daily operations; threat-level change; event">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4681_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4681_Task5" name="Design and operate the EP program: standing close-protection details scaled to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Design and operate the EP program: standing close-protection details scaled to each principal&#x27;s threat profile (W4678), protective logistics (vehicles, comms, medical), and the low-profile/high-profile posture toggle
Responsible (R): EP Lead
Accountable (A): CSO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4681_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4681_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4681_Task6" name="Execute daily EP operations: principal movements, venue/vehicle advance…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Execute daily EP operations: principal movements, venue/vehicle advance, protective surveillance and counter-surveillance, access control at principal engagements; coordinate with GSOC (W4676) and route security (W4683)
Responsible (R): EP Agents / EP Lead
Accountable (A): CSO
Duration: Daily</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4681_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4681_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4681_Task7" name="Review EP posture after each significant movement/event; capture lessons and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Review EP posture after each significant movement/event; capture lessons and adjust; maintain EP readiness drills (medical, evacuation, attack response)
Responsible (R): EP Lead / CSO
Accountable (A): CSO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4681_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4681_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4681_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4681_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4681_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-708 (ensure controlled execution — Executive Protection, Principal Travel &amp; Event Security (PA-159.2).) | - CTL-708: EP posture matches threat profile (W4678); drills maintained; GSOC coordination
Owner: EP Lead / CSO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W4681_Assoc10" sourceRef="W4681_Annotation9" targetRef="W4681_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W4681_Flow11" sourceRef="W4681_Start4" targetRef="W4681_Task5" />
