    <bpmn:process id="W_W4686" name="W4686. Kidnap &amp; Ransom (K&amp;R), Extortion &amp; Blackmail Response Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Kidnap/extortion/blackmail incident or credible threat
Frequency: Rare (rehearsal continuous)
Volume: ~ hopefully zero incidents; 1 rehearsed protocol
Owner: CSO / Crisis Response Lead
Participants: CEO, VP Legal (VS-100.3), CFO, K&amp;R insurer/consultant (VS-26), law enforcement (PNP/PNP-ACG/NBI), comms (VS-14.3), GSOC (W4676)
Source: workflow W4686 — Kidnap &amp; Ransom (K&amp;R), Extortion &amp; Blackmail Response Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4686_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4686_Lane1" name="CSO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4686_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4686_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4686_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4686_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4686_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4686_Start3" name="Kidnap/extortion/blackmail incident or credible threat">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4686_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4686_Task4" name="Maintain and rehearse the K&amp;R/extortion response protocol: incident activation…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Maintain and rehearse the K&amp;R/extortion response protocol: incident activation, crisis-response team, law-enforcement notification, K&amp;R insurer/consultant engagement (VS-26), negotiator coordination, and family/principal liaison — with strict information control
Responsible (R): CSO / Crisis Response Lead / K&amp;R Consultant
Accountable (A): CEO / VP Legal
Duration: Rehearsal continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4686_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4686_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4686_Task5" name="On incident: activate the protocol, engage law enforcement and K&amp;R consultant…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: On incident: activate the protocol, engage law enforcement and K&amp;R consultant, manage communications/information (avoid leakage that endangers the victim), and coordinate ransom/payment decisions per policy and law
Responsible (R): CSO / VP Legal / CFO / K&amp;R Consultant
Accountable (A): CEO / Board
Duration: Per incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4686_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4686_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4686_Task6" name="Conduct post-incident review (with the K&amp;R consultant and law enforcement)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Conduct post-incident review (with the K&amp;R consultant and law enforcement); capture lessons, support the victim/family recovery (VS-83), and adjust protocols and insurance (VS-26)
Responsible (R): CSO / VP Legal / K&amp;R Consultant
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Post-incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4686_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4686_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4686_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4686_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4686_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-708 (ensure controlled execution — Executive Protection, Principal Travel &amp; Event Security (PA-159.2).) | - CTL-708: K&amp;R protocol rehearsed; K&amp;R insurer/consultant engaged (VS-26); information control; Legal-guided payment decisions
Owner: CSO / Crisis Response Lead</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
