    <bpmn:process id="W_W4687" name="W4687. Employee Travel Risk, Pre-Travel Briefing &amp; Itinerary Tracking" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Employee/business trip (domestic inter-island or international)
Frequency: Per trip
Volume: ~300–500 tracked business trips/year (buyer/sourcing VS-122, executive, field-sales VS-140, audit VS-21, training)
Owner: Travel Risk Manager / CSO (joint with Travel/Mobility VS-160)
Participants: Travel booking (VS-160), HR (VS-19), managers, GSOC (W4676)
Source: workflow W4687 — Employee Travel Risk, Pre-Travel Briefing &amp; Itinerary Tracking</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4687_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4687_Lane1" name="Travel Risk Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4687_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4687_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4687_Lane2" name="Travel Risk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4687_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4687_Lane3" name="GSOC">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4687_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4687_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4687_Start5" name="Employee/business trip (domestic inter-island or international)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4687_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4687_Task6" name="For each business trip, screen the destination against travel-risk intelligence…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: For each business trip, screen the destination against travel-risk intelligence (W4679); require pre-travel briefing for elevated-risk destinations (threats, health, local laws, emergency contacts, check-in cadence)
Responsible (R): Travel Risk Manager / Mobility
Accountable (A): CSO / HR
Duration: Per trip</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4687_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4687_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4687_Task7" name="Enroll the traveler in itinerary tracking (linked to GSOC W4676) for the trip…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Enroll the traveler in itinerary tracking (linked to GSOC W4676) for the trip duration; confirm travel/medical insurance and K&amp;R coverage applicability (VS-26); brief duty-of-care obligations to the manager
Responsible (R): Travel Risk / Mobility / GSOC
Accountable (A): CSO
Duration: Per trip</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4687_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4687_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4687_Task8" name="Monitor active travelers for emerging destination threats (W4676); on threat…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Monitor active travelers for emerging destination threats (W4676); on threat, alert and advise (shelter, relocate, evacuate — W4688); debrief high-risk trips
Responsible (R): GSOC / Travel Risk
Accountable (A): CSO
Duration: Per active trip</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4687_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4687_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4687_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4687_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4687_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-708 (ensure controlled execution — Executive Protection, Principal Travel &amp; Event Security (PA-159.2).) | - CTL-708: elevated-risk trips briefed + tracked; duty-of-care documented; insurance confirmed
Owner: Travel Risk Manager / CSO (joint with Travel/Mobility VS-160)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
